nt Debate","description":"Contrast walled-garden copilots with open agent ecosystems as a strategic wedge for composable web advocates.","action":"Publish a take naming closed incumbents vs open alternatives, cite partner examples (Clerk, Neon), and invite ecosystem builders to reply.","frequency":"Monthly"},{"id":"biilmann-4","emoji":"🎤","title":"Conference & Partner Story","description":"Amplify stage talks and partnership narratives (Storyblok, JoyConf) that reinforce JAMstack/composable web leadership.","action":"Post 3 takeaways from a talk or partnership, tag partners, and attach a clip or slide with one quotable line on shipping fast.","frequency":"Monthly"},{"id":"biilmann-5","emoji":"🔧","title":"Builder-on-the-Metal Experiment","description":"Share personal builds and blog experiments (AI agents on his site, typographic tweaks) to stay credible as a hands-on CEO.","action":"Ship a small public experiment, document what broke (e.g., bot bans, agent auth), and thread lessons for teams designing AX.","frequency":"Weekly"}],"hooks":["We coined JAMstack. Now we're obsessing over AX — here's why","What is the shortest path for an agent to go from user input to URL in production?","Closed copilots vs open agents: which web do you want?","Every website already has an Agent Experience — most are bad","DX won the last decade. AX will win this one","[N]+ sites are deployed to Netlify from ChatGPT every day — because we designed for agents"],"angles":["Term-coining thought leadership (JAMstack → AX)","Agent Experience as developer-platform strategy","Open web and composable architecture advocacy","Shipping-speed and time-to-URL case studies","Ecosystem partner spotlights (auth, DB, CMS)","CEO-as-builder experiments with AI agents"]},"nousresearch":{"plays":[{"id":"nousresearch-1","emoji":"🧠","title":"Open-Weight Model Release","description":"Ship Hermes and other open models on Hugging Face with cards, benchmarks, and clear intended use cases.","action":"Announce relea