h community building","Hermes family as practical open agents/models","Technical reproducibility over marketing hype","Progress updates from a small lab competing with giants"]},"teknium":{"plays":[{"id":"teknium-1","emoji":"⚙️","title":"Training Run Postmortem","description":"Document fine-tuning decisions — data mix, hyperparams, failure modes — for Hermes and agent models.","action":"Post a technical thread with 6-10 bullets, link GitHub commit or config, and reply to HF/GitHub issues same day.","frequency":"Weekly"},{"id":"teknium-2","emoji":"🤖","title":"Hermes Agent Capability Demo","description":"Show real agent workflows (tool use, multi-step tasks) enabled by Nous engineering.","action":"Record a short demo or share logs of agent completing a task, note model version, and link hermes-agent.nousresearch.com resources.","frequency":"Weekly"},{"id":"teknium-3","emoji":"📂","title":"HF/GitHub Release Cadence","description":"Maintain high-velocity open releases so practitioners can fork, fine-tune, and deploy quickly.","action":"Push model card update or inference notebook, announce on X with '@' mentions to downstream integrators, and tag #opensource.","frequency":"Weekly"},{"id":"teknium-4","emoji":"🧪","title":"Ablation & Eval Deep Dive","description":"Share what was tried and removed — ablations, rejected datasets — to build credibility with ML engineers.","action":"Publish one ablation result chart, explain the negative result, and invite replication on HF Discussions.","frequency":"Monthly"},{"id":"teknium-5","emoji":"🛠️","title":"Practitioner Engineering Tips","description":"Translate Stability/Nous experience into actionable guidance on inference, quantization, and agent scaffolding.","action":"Post a 'here's the script/config that saved us X hours' snippet, paste minimal code, and link full repo.","frequency":"Weekly"}],"hooks":["We just shipped Hermes [model/agent] — here's the training recipe","This ablation failed — and that's why the final model is better","Lead engineer notes from building open agents at @NousResearch","From @StabilityAI to open agents: what actually matters in fine-tuning","New on Hugging Face: [artifact] — clone it and run today","If you're building agents, stop doing [common mistake] — do this instead"],"angles":["Open-source agent and model engineering logs","Fine-tuning transparency and reproducible configs","Hermes Agent as flagship technical showcase","Hugging Face/GitHub-first distribution","Practical inference and deployment guidance","Negative results and ablation honesty"]},"demishassabis":{"plays":[{"id":"demishassabis-1","emoji":"🏆","title":"Breakthrough Milestone Announcement","description":"Announce major DeepMind science/AI milestones (AlphaFold, Gemini capabilities, Nobel-linked work) with institutional gravity.","action":"Post official milestone with 2-3 sentence context, link to paper or blog, tag @GoogleDeepMind, avoid thread hype — let results speak.","frequency":"Monthly"},{"id":"demishassabis-2","emoji":"🧬","title":"AI-for-Science Spotlight","description":"Highlight Isomorphic Labs and DeepMind work applying AI to drug discovery and fundamental science.","action":"Share one disease-target or discovery vignette, cite collaborators, and link isomorphiclabs.com or deepmind.google research page.","frequency":"Monthly"},{"id":"demishassabis-3","emoji":"🎯","title":"AGI Vision Framing","description":"Articulate long-horizon AGI mission — understanding intelligence and reality — without product demo noise.","action":"Publish a short reflective post tying recent result to AGI path, use measured tone, and point to peer-reviewed source.","frequency":"Monthly"},{"id":"demishassabis-4","emoji":"🤝","title":"Team & Partner Credit","description":"Elevate researchers, institutions, and cross-lab collaborations rather than personal brand building.","action":"Quote-tweet DeepMind paper with congratulations to lead authors, add one plain-language implication for science/medicine.","frequency":"Weekly"},{"id":"demishassabis-5","emoji":"📜","title":"Paper & Prize Amplification","description":"Leverage Nobel Laureate credibility to amplify rigorous science communication on X.","action":"When major prizes or Nature/Science papers land, post a single high-signal tweet with 'what this means' for patients or physics.","frequency":"Monthly"}],"hooks":["Proud to share new results from @GoogleDeepMind on [problem]","AI is accelerating scientific discovery — today's example: [breakthrough]","Working toward AGI means understanding the fundamental nature of reality","At @IsomorphicLabs we're using AI to solve [disease challenge]","Congratulations to the team on [paper/award] — a step toward [mission]","Nobel-winning science meets AI: what we learned about [topic]"],"angles":["AGI development as long-horizon scientific mission","AI for fundamental science and drug discovery","Institutional milestone announcements over personal hot takes","AlphaFold/Isomorphic health impact storytelling","Research credit and team elevation","Measured visionary framing tied to peer-reviewed work"]},"karpathy":{"plays":[{"id":"karpathy-1","emoji":"🧵","title":"Long-Form Educational Thread","description":"Explain one ML/AI concept from first principles in a numbered X thread accessible to engineers.","action":"Draft 8-15 tweet thread with diagrams or ASCII, no product pitch, and pin it for 48 hours while engaging replies.","frequency":"Weekly"},{"id":"karpathy-2","emoji":"💻","title":"Minimal Repo Drop","description":"Release tiny, readable repos (nanoGPT, micrograd, llm.c) that teach by showing working code.","action":"Push GitHub repo or major update, tweet 'educational minimalism' angle with clone-and-run instructions in 3 lines.","frequency":"Monthly"},{"id":"karpathy-3","emoji":"🎥","title":"Zero-to-Hero Curriculum Push","description":"Promote video lecture series that walk from scratch to training neural nets.","action":"Share one lecture clip with chapter title, link playlist, and ask